  "title": "DVB-S2-TABLE: Fix duplicate field name and waveform_id display base in BCT table",
  "description": "## Fix duplicate field name and waveform_id display base in DVB-S2 table dissector\n\n### Summary\n\nTwo issues in the `dvb-s2_table` dissector for the `tx_type` descriptor in BCT table:\n\n1. The `tx_start_offset_2` field is registered with the display name and filter abbreviation copied and pasted exactly from `tx_start_offset_1`, so the two distinct part of the field are indistinguishable in the GUI and share a duplicate filter name.\n2. The `waveform_id` field is displayed in hexadecimal, whereas the standard enumerates waveform IDs in decimal.\n\n### Bug 1: duplicate field name\n\nIn `epan/dissectors/packet-dvb-s2-table.c`:\n\n```\n// tx_start_offset_2 - name and abbrev copied from tx_start_offset_1\n\n\n{&hf_dvb_s2_table_tx_type_tx_start_offset_2,\n  { \"Tx type tx start offset 1\", \"dvb-s2_table.tx_type.tx_start_offset_1\",\n    FT_UINT24, BASE_DEC, NULL, DVB_S2_TABLE_TX_TYPE_TX_START_OFFSET_MASK, NULL, HFILL} },\n```\n\nBoth the display name (`\"Tx type tx start offset 1\"`) and the filter abbreviation (`dvb-s2_table.tx_type.tx_start_offset_1`) duplicate `tx_start_offset_1`.\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```\n{&hf_dvb_s2_table_tx_type_tx_start_offset_2,\n  { \"Tx type tx start offset 2\", \"dvb-s2_table.tx_type.tx_start_offset_2\",\n    FT_UINT24, BASE_DEC, NULL, DVB_S2_TABLE_TX_TYPE_TX_START_OFFSET_MASK, NULL, HFILL} },\n```\n\n### Enhancement 1: waveform_id display base\n\nWaveform IDs are enumerated in decimal in the standard.\n\n`{&hf_dvb_s2_table_tx_type_waveform_id, { \"Tx type waveform id\", \"dvb-s2_table.tx_type.waveform_id\", FT_UINT8, BASE_HEX, NULL, 0x0, NULL, HFILL} },`\n\n**Fix:** `BASE_HEX` → `BASE_DEC`.\n\n### Standard reference\n\n**ETSI EN 301 545-2 V1.4.1** - waveform IDs in the `tx_type` descriptor are numbered in decimal, so decimal display matches the standard and it is easier to read.\n\n### Impact\n\n* The two parts of `tx_start_offset` fields can now be distinguished in the GUI and filtered independently.\n* `waveform_id` is shown in decimal, consistent with the standard's numbering.",
